.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# MLflow local backends (regenerated by the run scripts). The live/scheduled
# backend is the exception: the drift-loop workflow force-adds it to persist it.
mlflow*.db
mlartifacts*/
mlruns/

# Raw Open-Meteo observations are COMMITTED, not ignored: this is the real data
# we gather, so we keep it versioned rather than re-fetching (and possibly losing)
# it. The pages/scheduled workflows rebuild from this cache.

# Generated analysis outputs. `outputs/*` rather than `outputs/`, because git
# will not descend into an excluded directory and the negations below would
# never be consulted.
outputs/*

# Two exceptions, committed on purpose. The model ablation is an expensive
# two-city, three-arm replay that does not change from week to week, so the
# weekly site build reads this snapshot instead of re-running it -- which would
# add six replays and a hyper-parameter search to every Monday's job for a
# result nobody re-ran.
#
# A snapshot can go stale silently, so it is checked rather than trusted:
# `build_site.py` re-derives the untouched Ridge arm's premium and compares it
# against the premium that same build just measured for the city. Where they
# disagree the page draws no charts and says why, and
# `tests/test_site_assets.py` fails the build first. Re-run with
# `python scripts/ablate_model.py` when the loop changes.
!outputs/model_ablation.csv
!outputs/model_ablation_series.json

# Static site: the shell (index.html, app.js) is committed; the data files
# (data.json, one raw-data CSV per city) are generated at build time and
# published. The glob covers cities added later without another edit here.
site/data.json
site/*_hourly.csv

# Working notes, both private. HANDOFF.md carries the engineering facts that stay
# true across sessions, the ones a reader of the code could not work out for
# themselves; SESSION.md carries one session's narrative and the threads it left
# hanging, and stops being interesting once those close. Neither is a document
# this repository's readers need, and both are candid about work that is on
# display in the README, so neither belongs in the history.
#
# HANDOFF.md was tracked until 2026-08-13 and this rule did nothing, because git
# does not apply ignore rules to files it is already tracking. Untracked with
# `git rm --cached`; its earlier commits are still in the history behind us.
/SESSION.md
HANDOFF.md

# Cross-project working notes: the practices this project taught, kept as a
# personal record rather than a published document. It is self-critical about
# work that is on display in the README, and the canonical copy now travels with
# whichever project is current. Documents that stay here are the ones a reader
# of this repository needs.
docs/PRACTICES.md
